1
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,320
Everyone, attack!

2
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:39,940
Yeah!

3
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,320
Yeah!

4
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,720
Yeah! Yeah!

5
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:15,737
I'm not sure you're gonna keep it.

6
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:18,377
I don't know what not.

7
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:22,657
I'm afraid of my fear.

8
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:24,328
I'm in the back of my head.

9
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:26,637
I'm in the same way.

10
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:31,017
I'm in the

11
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,740
same way.

12
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:36,997
I'm in the same way.

13
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:40,780
Here is the most beautiful place.

14
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:44,017
I'm in the same way.

15
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:48,100
I'm so happy with my body.

16
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:52,357
What if I'm feeling, I don't want this?

17
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:56,197
I'm so happy with my heart.

18
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:59,257
I'm so happy with my eyes.

19
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:03,557
You'll see it in my house.

20
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:07,597
I'm so happy when you
feel like I'm feeling.

21
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:10,697
I'm so happy with my feelings.

22
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:13,997
I'm so happy with you.

23
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,280
So A-N-D-S.

24
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,117
I wanna always do with you.

25
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,100
I'm giving you everything I have.

26
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,980
How many did we lose?

27
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,160
14 of us died.

28
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,460
Oh my god!

29
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:58,937
And we still got 25 floors to go.

30
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:00,837
25 more floors?

31
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:03,744
How the hell are we even
gonna make it that far?

32
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:43,300
Kirito, what are you...

33
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,300
An immortal object?

34
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,960
Commander Heathcliff, what's going on?

35
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,480
I think I got the answer to that.

36
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,057
Reason why the Commander's HP never hits

37
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:05,905
yellow is because he's
protected by the system.

38
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:12,184
You know, ever since day one, something's
always bugged me about this whole thing.

39
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:14,537
I was always wondering,

40
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:18,937
where is he hiding while he watches us
and controls everything in this world?

41
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,320
Well, the answer's pretty simple.

42
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,400
It's basic psychology.

43
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:27,240
In fact, it's so simple
every kid knows it.

44
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:31,501
There's nothing more boring than
watching someone else play an RPG.

45
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:35,440
Is there, Akihiko Kayaba?

46
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:43,217
Just for my curiosity's sake, would you
mind telling me how you figured it out?

47
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:46,771
The first time I knew something
was up was during our duel.

48
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,317
Remember when you turned the tables on me?

49
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,200
That move was way too fast.

50
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:54,300
Yes, I thought so.

51
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:57,597
It was a mistake to think that
would go unnoticed by you.

52
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:59,757
But you were so strong and so fast,

53
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:03,428
the only choice I had was to
engage the system's assist mode.

54
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,917
Yes, I am Akihiko Kayaba.

55
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,412
And now that my identity's been revealed,

56
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:17,895
it should come as no surprise that I
am the final boss on the top floor.

57
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:25,140
So the strongest player in the whole
game ends up being the final boss.

58
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:26,911
Kind of cliche, isn't it?

59
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,318
Actually, I kind of like that angle.

60
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:31,457
One thing's for sure,

61
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:34,997
I always thought you'd be the one
standing before me at the very end.

62
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:37,337
You know, dual wielding is a rare skill,

63
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:40,917
the kind that's only given to the
player with the fastest reaction time.

64
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,760
He is the hero of this story, the one
who rises up to challenge the Demon King.

65
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:49,920
But you, the power you've
displayed exceeded my expectations.

66
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:52,737
I guess these unexpected twists and turns

67
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:56,260
are what makes MMORPG
so thrilling to play.

68
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,540
Our loyalty, our hope.

69
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,630
Paralysis.

70
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,070
Kirito!

71
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,640
What's the plan now, huh?

72
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:26,010
Huh?

73
00:06:26,093 --> 00:06:27,857
You gonna kill everyone here
and cover it up or something?

74
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:28,920
Oh, God, no.

75
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:31,977
That wouldn't be sporting
of me, now would it?

76
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:33,760
No, I have a better idea.

77
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:37,497
I'm going to head for the top floor
and wait for all of you there.

78
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,404
I'll be inside the Ruby Palace.

79
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,257
It's a shame I have to
leave you all so soon.

80
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,357
I've spent lots of time
developing the Knights

81
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,911
of the Blood Oath and other elite players.

82
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:48,290
Oh, well.

83
00:06:48,373 --> 00:06:51,671
You're all strong, so I'm sure
you'll reach me, eventually.

84
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:53,940
But before I go...

85
00:06:55,820 --> 00:07:00,157
Kirito, I feel you deserve some kind
of reward for discovering my identity,

86
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,140
so I'll give you a chance.

87
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,320
Chance for what?

88
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:06,420
To fight me one-on-one,
right here, right now.

89
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,540
Oh, and my immortality
will be deactivated.

90
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,297
Defeat me and you clear the game,

91
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:15,497
and all of the players will be
able to log out from this world.

92
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,697
No strings attached.

93
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:17,820
What do you say?

94
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,600
Don't do it, Kirito.

95
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:21,920
I don't like it.

96
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,276
We should fall back.

97
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:27,350
Oh,

98
00:07:27,433 --> 00:07:28,263
my

99
00:07:28,346 --> 00:07:33,560
God.

100
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:54,770
I have to.

101
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:59,720
Okay then, let's finish it. Kirito.

102
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:03,920
I'm sorry, I can't run away
if it means ending this.

103
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:07,680
You better not die, you hear me?

104
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:10,260
No, I'm gonna win.

105
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,160
I promise I'm gonna end this world.

106
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,820
Okay, I believe in you, Kirito.

107
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:30,420
Kirito! Don't! Kirito!

108
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,050
Hey, Gil.

109
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:39,505
Thanks for supporting all the
players in the game since day one.

110
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,180
Yeah, I knew.

111
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:43,357
You act like you're all about the money,

112
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,457
but I know you spent
every penny you had on

113
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:48,011
helping the intermediate players level up.

114
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:50,530
Klein?

115
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:54,500
I'm sorry I bailed on you that day.

116
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,500
I think about it all the time.

117
00:08:59,380 --> 00:09:00,420
Dammit, Kittito!

118
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,240
Don't you apologize!

119
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,680
Don't you dare apologize now!

120
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,500
I won't accept it!

121
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:10,977
I'll never accept it until we're on the
other side and you're buying me dinner,

122
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:11,940
goddammit!

123
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:13,080
You got it.

124
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,149
See you on the other side.

125
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:26,620
If it's okay, I have a final
request to make. What is it?

126
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,100
I'm not planning on going down easy.

127
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:31,140
So if I die today,

128
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:36,020
I want your word that you'll fix
it so Asuna doesn't kill herself.

129
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,460
As you wish.

130
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,767
No, Kirito, that's not fair!

131
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:43,020
You can't do that!

132
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,640
It's not fair! No!

133
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,780
This isn't some in-game duel.

134
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,040
It's a fight to the death.

135
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,720
That's fine with me.

136
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,380
Because I'm going to kill him.

137
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:16,920
He can block whatever I throw at him.

138
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:19,217
Because he designed the
dual-wielding skill.

139
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:21,380
and he knows all its combos.

140
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:26,220
I have to beat him with my own power
without using the sword skills.

141
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,430
Faster.

142
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,900
I gotta go faster! Oh!

143
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:04,000
I'm sorry, Asuna.

144
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,680
Please, keep living.

145
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,580
Game over, Kirito.

146
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:49,540
Asuna, Asuna, you can't, you can't be.

147
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,000
I'm sorry.

148
00:11:58,020 --> 00:11:59,100
Goodbye.

149
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:21,377
Now that was a surprise!

150
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:25,757
I'm sure I never programmed a way for
players to neutralize their own paralysis.

151
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:28,980
I guess sometimes these
things just happen.

152
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,570
Hmm?

153
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:22,580
It's over now.

154
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:29,340
I believe in you, Kirito.

155
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,340
Not yet.

156
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,260
Not yet.

157
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:21,800
We did it, didn't we?

158
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:29,820
PHONE RINGS

159
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:01,300
On November 7th at 2.55pm,
the game has been cleared.

160
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:04,280
Repeat, the game has been cleared.

161
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:22,280
Where am I?

162
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:35,880
Kitty-dough. Kitty-dough.

163
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:51,440
I'm sorry.

164
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,885
I guess I ended up dying, too.

165
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:55,710
Dummy.

166
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,480
Where are we?

167
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,020
Do you know?

168
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,560
A stunning view, isn't it?

169
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,820
Akihiko Kayaba.

170
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,100
At Argus headquarters,

171
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:48,057
the SAO mainframe is in a room
five floors below street level.

172
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:51,493
and right now it's deleting
all the data from its drives.

173
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:57,160
In about ten minutes, everything in
this world will disappear forever.

174
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,820
And all the players?

175
00:17:00,160 --> 00:17:01,440
What happens to them?

176
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:04,679
You don't have to worry about them.

177
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:11,420
The 6,147 players who survived the game up
to now were logged out a few seconds ago.

178
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,880
And what about the 4,000 people who died?

179
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,580
What about them?

180
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:20,060
They'll never return.

181
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:24,660
In any world, real or virtual,
once you're dead, you're gone.

182
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:29,450
Why?

183
00:17:29,533 --> 00:17:30,363
What's the point?

184
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:31,780
Why did you do this?

185
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,820
That's a good question.

186
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,308
It's been so long I've
forgotten the reason.

187
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:39,620
Isn't that strange?

188
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:45,397
Even before I developed a system for the
full-dive environment, I dreamed of this.

189
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:50,360
A castle in a world that wasn't governed
by earthly laws and restrictions.

190
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:54,001
I poured my life into
making that world a reality.

191
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,737
I created this world,

192
00:17:57,820 --> 00:18:02,526
and I got to see something that surpassed
anything I could have imagined for it.

193
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:07,560
My steel castle, floating in the sky.

194
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:11,527
I don't remember how old I was
when I became obsessed with it.

195
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:15,660
I wanted to leave the earth,
to fly to that castle.

196
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:20,700
I wanted that more than anything
else, for as long as I can remember.

197
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,440
You know what, Kirito?

198
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:29,494
I want to believe it's still out there.

199
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:34,860
That somewhere in some other world, my
castle is still standing, taller than ever.

200
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:39,560
Yeah, maybe it still is.

201
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:51,780
Before I forget, congratulations on
clearing the game, Kirito, Asuna.

202
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:58,840
Well then, I should
probably get going now.

203
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:19,620
Guess this is goodbye.

204
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,860
This isn't goodbye at all!

205
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:26,317
We're gonna be together
when we finally disappear.

206
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:28,820
So we're gonna be together forever.

207
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:32,257
Hey, you never told me your real name?

208
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:34,700
Would you please tell me before we go?

209
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,030
Kazuto

210
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:43,180
Kazuto Kirigaya And
last month, I turned 16.

211
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:45,840
Kazuto Kirigaya.

212
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:49,180
So you're younger than me, huh?

213
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,760
My name is Asuna Yuki.

214
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:54,540
I'm 17 now.

215
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,540
Asuna Yuki.

216
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:59,060
Asuna Yuki.

217
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:07,160
Sorry.

218
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:08,650
Sorry.

219
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:09,957
I swore.

220
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:15,377
I promised I'd save you, get you
back to the real world, but I...

221
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:17,400
I couldn't.

222
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:22,717
It's okay.

223
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:23,780
It's okay.

224
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:29,900
I'm happy I got to meet you, Kazuto, and
to be with you, and to live with you.

225
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:33,460
This is the happiest I've
ever been in my whole life.

226
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:37,000
Thank you for that, and I love you.

227
00:20:56,480 --> 00:21:00,240
I love you so very much.

228
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:29,880
Oh, my God.

229
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:04,240
Oh, Sue.

230
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:15,720
Oh, I'm sorry.

231
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:45,800
It's just the reality that the reality is.

232
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:54,297
I've been looking forward

233
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:55,597
to seeing the future.

234
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:58,445
I've been looking forward
to seeing the future.

235
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:03,017
I've been looking forward

236
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:07,660
to seeing the future.
The world's infinite.

237
00:23:10,880 --> 00:23:12,577
Even if it's a dream.

238
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:14,697
Even if it's too late.

239
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:17,000
Even if it's too late.

240
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:36,830
It's always, always.

241
00:23:36,913 --> 00:23:38,220
Next time, return.
